========================================================================
(2) LAW on primitive 5-sets: full-support debt ZERO <=> not sign-reachable mod3 <=> k=1
========================================================================
  tested 401 primitive 5-sets; law holds 400/401
  full-support DEBT-FREE sets (all have k=1, one runner !=0 mod3): [((1, 3, 6, 12, 15), 1), ((3, 9, 12, 13, 15), 1), ((3, 9, 10, 12, 15), 1)]

========================================================================
(3) mod-6 sign refinement: same mod-3 channels, different mod-2 signs -> different debt
========================================================================
  (1, 2, 4, 5, 7) (mod6=[1, 2, 4, 5, 1]) debt=-0.002140
  (1, 2, 4, 5, 1) (mod6=[1, 2, 4, 5, 1]) debt=-0.007414   (value differs -> mod-6 matters)
  (1, 2, 4, 5, 7) (mod6=[1, 2, 4, 5, 1]) debt=-0.002140
  (4, 5, 1, 2, 7) (mod6=[4, 5, 1, 2, 1]) debt=-0.002140   (same)
  (1, 1, 1, 2, 2) (mod6=[1, 1, 1, 2, 2]) debt=-0.019632
  (4, 4, 4, 5, 5) (mod6=[4, 4, 4, 5, 5]) debt=-0.016318   (value differs -> mod-6 matters)
  => feasibility is mod-3 (the 3 channels); the debt VALUE/sign is mod-6
     (each ghat(m) sign set by m mod 6). mod6 = mod3-channel (x) mod2-sign-unit.

========================================================================
(4) n=4 parallel (units mod 2 = {1}: one fixed sum, 'a+b+c odd')
========================================================================
   (a,b,c)=(1, 2, 3) sum=6 (even) full debt=-0.075029 -> PRESENT
   (a,b,c)=(1, 2, 4) sum=7 (odd) full debt=+0.000000 -> ZERO
   (a,b,c)=(1, 3, 5) sum=9 (odd) full debt=+0.000000 -> ZERO
   (a,b,c)=(2, 3, 5) sum=10 (even) full debt=-0.066203 -> PRESENT
   n=4: debt-free <=> a+b+c ODD (units {1}, no sign freedom: ONE channel).
   n=6: debt-free <=> NO eps in {+-1}^5 with sum eps_i v_i = 0 mod 3
        (units {+-1}: a sign per runner over 3 channels) = FIRST multi-channel law.
